<wpt lat="40.346330" lon="-1.062030"><name>DZC Mansueto fort (Valdecebro)</name><desc>Valdecebro · 1937–1938

Mansueto is a promontory guarding the south-eastern approach to Teruel above Valdecebro. The Republicans fortified it not with the usual sandbagged trenches but with a small fort of thick concrete and brick walls, roofed with a concrete slab on railway rails. It formed part of the Republican ring around Teruel.

Broken wall sections with firing loopholes and fragments of the concrete roof.

It is a short walk from Valdecebro, about 5 km east of Teruel. The site is ruined, so watch your footing.

Accuracy: HIGH — exact spot known.

