<wpt lat="40.297000" lon="-1.111800"><name>DZC Muela de Villaspesa</name><desc>Villaspesa · 1937–1938

The Muela de Villaspesa was an intermediate fortified point south of Teruel overlooking the Republican positions at Aldehuela and the Turia valley. Its defenders dug a tunnel from the trench line to the back of the hill so they could move without being seen or hit from the Republican positions at Las Cañadas.

Trenches and observation posts on the slope facing Aldehuela, and the tunnel, whose rear entrance is now sealed.

It is near Villaspesa, about 8 km south of Teruel. Open hillside, so bring boots. Combine it with the Aldehuela bunker opposite.

Accuracy: MEDIUM — right area, exact spot uncertain.

