<wpt lat="37.357000" lon="-6.004000"><name>DZC Tablada airfield (Army of Africa airlift), Seville</name><desc>Seville · Late Jul – Oct 1936

With the Republican navy blocking the Strait, Franco's Army of Africa was stuck in Morocco. From late July 1936 German Junkers Ju 52 and Italian Savoia-Marchetti transports flew legionnaires and Regulares from Tetuán to Seville — the first large military airlift in history, landing mainly at Tablada and at Jerez. The troops then marched north to Badajoz and Madrid. The airfield was a military base and aviation school afterwards.

A military base; only its perimeter can be seen.

View from outside only.

Accuracy: LOW — general area only.

Private land — view from the road.

